WEBVTT

00:01:55.563 --> 00:02:00.799
CA: In this episode, David and I are going
to explore how these new ideas connect,

00:02:00.823 --> 00:02:03.002
both the quest for personal meaning

00:02:03.026 --> 00:02:05.425
and the dream of political renewal

00:02:05.449 --> 00:02:08.413
anchored in a new focus on neighborhood.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:13.979
David will share why he’s inspired
by a group of people he calls "weavers,"

00:02:14.003 --> 00:02:16.401
for moral and political answers.

00:02:18.226 --> 00:02:19.643
David Brooks, welcome.

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:20.818
DB: Good to be with you.

00:02:20.842 --> 00:02:23.819
CA: So, I'm really intrigued
by this conversation,

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:28.470
because I see you as one of
the great synthesizers of different ideas.

00:02:28.494 --> 00:02:31.688
It's always amazed me
how you can combine thinking